✅ QUESTION 1: 3SUM

(NOT in your list)

🔹 Problem

Given an integer array nums, return all unique triplets [a,b,c] such that:
a + b + c = 0

🔹 Algorithm

Sort the array.

Fix one element i.

Use two pointers left and right.

If sum == 0 → store triplet.

If sum < 0 → move left.

If sum > 0 → move right.

Skip duplicates.

⏱ Time: O(n²)
📦 Space: O(1)

🔹 Java Code
import java.util.*;

class ThreeSum {
    public static List<List<Integer>> threeSum(int[] nums) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length - 2; i++) {
            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) continue;

            int left = i + 1;
            int right = nums.length - 1;

            while (left < right) {
                int sum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];

                if (sum == 0) {
                    result.add(Arrays.asList(nums[i], nums[left], nums[right]));
                    left++;
                    right--;

                    while (left < right && nums[left] == nums[left - 1]) left++;
                    while (left < right && nums[right] == nums[right + 1]) right--;
                } else if (sum < 0) {
                    left++;
                } else {
                    right--;
                }
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
}

🔹 Sample Input
nums = [-1,0,1,2,-1,-4]

🔹 Output
[[-1, -1, 2], [-1, 0, 1]]

🔹 Line-by-Line Explanation

Arrays.sort(nums); → allows two-pointer approach

for (int i = 0...) → fix first element

if duplicate → continue → avoid repeated answers

left & right → scan remaining array

sum == 0 → valid triplet

Skip duplicates to avoid repetition
